# Local CI Parity

Husky splits local gates (F62 / #182): **pre-push stays lean** (lint + unit tests);
**pre-commit** runs typecheck + security-scan + job_type dispatch. **Full CI parity only
before opening a PR**. GitHub Actions remains the merge gate.

## When to run what

| When | Command | What |
|------|---------|------|
| While editing | Hooks (auto) | `format` + `lint-fix` + scoped typecheck on edited file |
| Agent stop | `make check-fast` + `make test-fast` | Lint + typecheck; scoped unit tests |
| **git commit** (Husky) | `scripts/ci/pre_commit.sh` | Typecheck + security-scan + job-dispatch |
| **git push** (Husky) | `make lint` + `make test-fast` | Lint + scoped unit tests only |
| Before commit (manual) | `make check` | Lint + format-check + typecheck |
| **Before opening PR** | `make ci-push` or `make ci-pr-ready` | Full CI parity locally |

Hook scripts: `.cursor/hooks/make_format_lint_fix.py`, `.cursor/hooks/typecheck.py`,
`.cursor/hooks/make_ci_on_stop.py`.

Stop-hook failures are **advisory** (do not block ending the session).

## Tier 1 — Lean push + agent stop

| When | Command | What |
|------|---------|------|
| After save | Hooks | `format` + `lint-fix` + scoped `typecheck` on edited file |
| Agent stop | `make check-fast` + `make test-fast` | Lint + typecheck; unit tests for changed components only |
| git push | `make lint` + `make test-fast` | **No** typecheck / security-scan on push |

## Tier 2 — Pre-commit (Husky) + optional medium push

```bash
# Husky pre-commit (default on every commit):
make typecheck
make security-scan
# + scripts/ci/pre_commit_job_dispatch.sh

make check          # manual: lint + format-check + typecheck
make test-fast      # scoped unit tests
```

Format-check, audit, full pytest, coverage gate, and frontend production builds stay on
`make ci-push` / GitHub CI — not on pre-commit by default.

Opt-in medium pre-push: `VECINITA_MEDIUM_PRE_PUSH=1 git push` (adds format-check via `make check`).

Skip hooks: `VECINITA_SKIP_PRE_COMMIT=1`, `VECINITA_SKIP_PRE_PUSH=1`.

## Tier 3 — Full (before PR; optional on push)

```bash
make ci-push        # or: make ci-pr-ready
```

Includes: `ci-guards`, lint, format-check, typecheck, audit, full pytest, both Vitest suites,
unit coverage gate, frontend production build.

Run manually **before marking a PR ready for review**. GitHub CI runs the same checks on push.

Opt-in full parity on every push: `VECINITA_FULL_PRE_PUSH=1 git push`.

Skip pre-push entirely (emergencies only): `VECINITA_SKIP_PRE_PUSH=1 git push`.

`make ci` still includes `install` for explicit full local runs; `ci-push` skips reinstall.

## Agent must fix manually

Issues hooks cannot auto-fix: type errors, non-auto-fixable lint, test failures, CI guards, audit CVEs.

## Reference

Full GitHub parity: `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (+ `deploy-preflight.yml` on `main` push).
Release tags after DO CD: `.github/workflows/release.yml` (F63 / #103).
